A declaration keyword alone on its line (:PARAMETERS, :DECLARE) takes its
operand list from the following lines: no `;` is forced after the bare
keyword (fmt.semicolon_enforcement issue #216), and every list line takes
one continuation level, as the operand of a keyword that ended the
previous line does (fmt.indent_style, issue #326).
-- input.ssl --
:PROCEDURE ChartStats;
:PARAMETERS
sChartId, aRules,
nMean;
:DEFAULT sChartId, "";
:DECLARE
nIndex, nCount;
nIndex := Len(aRules);
nCount := nMean;
:RETURN nCount + nIndex;
:ENDPROC;
-- format --
:PROCEDURE ChartStats;
	:PARAMETERS
		sChartId, aRules,
		nMean;
	:DEFAULT sChartId, "";
	:DECLARE
		nIndex, nCount;
	nIndex := Len(aRules);
	nCount := nMean;
	:RETURN nCount + nIndex;
:ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
